WINDOWS 10 INSTALLATION GUIDE
==============================

1. PREPARE BEFORE INSTALLATION
------------------------------
[ ] Back up important files to an external drive or cloud storage.
[ ] Keep the laptop connected to AC power.
[ ] Prepare a Windows 10 installation USB (8 GB or larger).
[ ] Keep your Windows product key available if required.
[ ] Check laptop compatibility and download important drivers.

2. BOOT FROM WINDOWS 10 USB
---------------------------
[ ] Insert the Windows 10 USB drive.
[ ] Restart the laptop.
[ ] Open the Boot Menu or BIOS/UEFI.
[ ] Common keys: F12, F9, ESC, DEL.
[ ] Select the USB drive as the boot device.
[ ] Boot from the USB when prompted.

3. START WINDOWS SETUP
----------------------
[ ] Select language, time/currency and keyboard layout.
[ ] Click NEXT.
[ ] Select INSTALL NOW.
[ ] Enter the product key.
[ ] Or select I DON'T HAVE A PRODUCT KEY.
[ ] Select the correct Windows 10 edition.
[ ] Accept the license terms.
[ ] Select CUSTOM: INSTALL WINDOWS ONLY (ADVANCED).

4. PARTITION THE DRIVE
----------------------
[ ] Identify the correct internal drive.
[ ] Make sure important data is backed up.
[ ] Delete old partitions only if a clean installation is required.
[ ] Select the UNALLOCATED SPACE.
[ ] Click NEW if you want to create partitions manually.
[ ] Leave enough space for Windows, apps and updates.
[ ] For a simple setup, select unallocated space and click NEXT.
[ ] Windows will create the required system partitions automatically.
[ ] Do not delete recovery/manufacturer partitions unless necessary.

5. INSTALL WINDOWS
------------------
[ ] Select the partition for Windows.
[ ] Click NEXT.
[ ] Wait while Windows copies files and installs.
[ ] The laptop will restart several times.
[ ] Remove the USB if the laptop starts the installer again.
[ ] Complete the initial Windows setup.

6. PRIVACY SETTINGS
-------------------
[ ] Review LOCATION access.
[ ] Disable location if it is not needed.
[ ] Review DIAGNOSTIC DATA settings.
[ ] Choose the more privacy-conscious option available.
[ ] Review ADVERTISING ID settings.
[ ] Review speech, typing and personalization settings.
[ ] Disable unnecessary app permissions.

AFTER REACHING THE DESKTOP:
[ ] Open SETTINGS > PRIVACY.
[ ] Review Camera permissions.
[ ] Review Microphone permissions.
[ ] Review Location permissions.
[ ] Review Contacts and other personal-information permissions.
[ ] Allow access only to apps that need it.

7. INSTALL UPDATES AND DRIVERS
------------------------------
[ ] Open SETTINGS > UPDATE & SECURITY > WINDOWS UPDATE.
[ ] Click CHECK FOR UPDATES.
[ ] Install available Windows updates.
[ ] Restart when required.
[ ] Check for updates again.
[ ] Install laptop-specific drivers from the manufacturer's official website.
[ ] Open DEVICE MANAGER.
[ ] Check for warning icons.
[ ] Install missing drivers for Wi-Fi, graphics, audio, chipset and touchpad.

8. POST-INSTALLATION CHECKS
---------------------------
[ ] Test Wi-Fi.
[ ] Test Bluetooth.
[ ] Test speakers.
[ ] Test microphone.
[ ] Test webcam.
[ ] Test keyboard.
[ ] Test touchpad.
[ ] Check display resolution.
[ ] Check Windows activation.
[ ] Install required applications.
[ ] Confirm Windows Security is active.
[ ] Create a restore point.
[ ] Back up important files.

PARTITIONING TIPS
-----------------
[ ] Keep personal files separate from Windows if useful.
[ ] Do not make the Windows partition too small.
[ ] Leave free space for updates and applications.
[ ] If unsure, let Windows create its required partitions automatically.
[ ] Never delete a partition without knowing what it contains.
[ ] Always back up important data before changing partitions.

STEPS THAT MAY BE UNCLEAR OR MISSING
------------------------------------
1. BOOT MENU KEY
   The exact key depends on the laptop manufacturer and model.

2. UEFI OR LEGACY MODE
   Older laptops may use different firmware settings.

3. STORAGE DRIVER
   Some laptops may require a storage-controller driver before
   Windows Setup can detect the SSD.

4. WINDOWS ACTIVATION
   Activation depends on whether the laptop has a digital license
   or a product key.

5. RECOVERY PARTITION
   Deleting it may remove the manufacturer's recovery option.

6. WINDOWS 10 SUPPORT
   Windows 10 reached standard end of support on October 14, 2025.
   In 2026, use Windows 10 only when there is a specific compatibility
   or legacy-software reason. A supported Windows version is preferable.

FINAL RESULT
------------
[ ] Windows starts normally.
[ ] Correct drivers are installed.
[ ] Windows is activated.
[ ] Privacy settings have been reviewed.
[ ] Available updates are installed.
[ ] Hardware has been tested.
